{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuihAANE3g4RwiWrt6db","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, that has changed. According to a Cloudflare changelog entry from September 4, 2026, the 3 MB (Free) and 10 MB (Paid) compressed limits were removed. Workers now have one limit of **64 MiB uncompressed** on both Free and Paid plans, and the Workers Limits page shows the same figure. When you run a dry-run deploy, the uncompressed \"Total Upload\" size is the number that counts; the gzip size is only for information. The Workflows limits page still lists 3 MB/10 MB, but it looks out of date. These details come from the search result summaries; I didn't open the pages themselves.\n\nSources:\n- [Limits · Cloudflare Workers docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/)\n- [Deploy larger Workers — up to 64 MiB for both free and paid plans · Changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-09-04-increased-worker-size-limit/)\n- [Limits · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/limits/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1178,"cache_read_input_tokens":22282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1178},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bc7c7bf-0ecb-46e3-8870-df07edda2d72","uuid":"4c0045b2-621c-4d0d-8808-6ac2afc78481","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:13:07.617Z","request_id":"req_011Cfuih9uFCvEdUQLMmDR1q"}
